# Redis-flavored dev overlay — loaded BEFORE .env.dev by `task dev:redis`.
#
# Sets only one variable: `MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES` (the redis-transport
# variant). The full directive value is redefined here rather than
# composed from .env.dev because dotenv has no per-key merge — to swap
# the `transport` block, the entire `MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES` string
# must be replaced. Non-transport vars (JWT keys, SERVER_NAME,
# MERCURE_HUB_NAME, GLOBAL_OPTIONS, CADDY_*) are NOT defined here and
# fall through to .env.dev.
#
# Loaded via `dotenv: ['.env.local', '.env.dev.redis', '.env.dev']` on the
# `dev:redis` task. go-task applies dotenv files with FIRST-WINS semantics
# (earlier files take precedence; later files only fill in unset vars),
# so the order is intentional: .env.local overrides .env.dev.redis
# overrides .env.dev. The `MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES` value here wins over
# .env.dev's bolt-flavored value because this file is listed first.
#
# `.env.dev` should NOT carry a duplicate `transport redis {...}` block.
# Single source of truth — this file. `.env.dev` points here via comment.
#
# WARNING: DEVELOPMENT ONLY — same disclaimer as .env.dev. Do not use
# these JWT secrets / origins in production.

MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES="
cors_origins http://localhost:63342 https://localhost:63342 https://localhost
publish_origins *
demo
subscriptions
anonymous
ui
transport redis {
    url redis://localhost:6379
    stream mercure
    max_length 10000
    encoding json
    event_ttl 24h
    cleanup_interval 5m
}
heartbeat 15s
write_timeout 300s"
